			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"labelPosition": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "8KT8M6Bo",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 1558.8726506413573,
			"y": 939.4851951341323,
			"width": 511.38671875,
			"height": 225,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "at",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 437857187,
			"version": 405,
			"versionNonce": 1498188333,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1794329573841,
			"created": 1794326457866,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "DeepDive : Security Problem\nWhat if attacker invents a auth token that not on blacklist, \nhow backend rejects it\n-> check expiry, issuer, intended audience, + revocation\n\nIncorrect money movement?\n-> Scheduler job to do reconsilation every 12pm\n-> debit==credit\n-> ",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"baseFontSize": null,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "DeepDive : Security Problem\nWhat if attacker invents a auth token that not on blacklist, \nhow backend rejects it\n-> check expiry, issuer, intended audience, + revocation\n\nIncorrect money movement?\n-> Scheduler job to do reconsilation every 12pm\n-> debit==credit\n-> ",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"labelPosition": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "KDViOgC7",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 1917.9983189239933,
			"y": 1184.1277953318381,
			"width": 800,
			"height": 1100,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "au",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 352077453,
			"version": 1577,
			"versionNonce": 1022672013,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1794329573841,
			"created": 1794326809564,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Trade Offs\nWhy use microservices?\nTrade off \n- simplicity\n+ complexity\n+ availablility\n+ effort to coordinate\n+ monitoring cost\n\nWould upgrade service machines improve throughput even db is saturated?\n-> table sharding, horizontally scaling db\n-> user id as partition key\n\nAtomicity debit 2 record on different db?\n-> redis distribute key / 2 phase commit\n\nWhat if one crash?\n-> 2 phase commit, one coordinator check is both db prepared\n-> only prepared only do commit or rollback\n\nIs sharding neccesary?\n-> Load test it with reality data volumes, concurrent transfers \nand balances and hisort loads. Only decide to sharding if they exceed our\nrequirments\n\nBottleneck for row locking design for hot wallet?\n->higher latency since more lock on same wallet\n-> fix? reduce RPC call, choose to not use msg queue\n\nIf merchant holds every db conncection on one row lock?\n-> Bounced time out, reject as temporarily busy\n\n-> Since after time out, client will keep retrying, fix?\n--> use rate limiting -> token refilling-> redis Lua Script, limit by walletID (for hot\nwallet)\n--> client use backoff retry\n\nWhat if all merchant retry?\n-> Use exponential backoff with random jitter, cap retries, and reuse original\nidemp key. Return too many request Record 429\n\n\n\n",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"baseFontSize": null,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Trade Offs\nWhy use microservices?\nTrade off \n- simplicity\n+ complexity\n+ availablility\n+ effort to coordinate\n+ monitoring cost\n\nWould upgrade service machines improve throughput even db is saturated?\n-> table sharding, horizontally scaling db\n-> user id as partition key\n\nAtomicity debit 2 record on different db?\n-> redis distribute key / 2 phase commit\n\nWhat if one crash?\n-> 2 phase commit, one coordinator check is both db prepared\n-> only prepared only do commit or rollback\n\nIs sharding neccesary?\n-> Load test it with reality data volumes, concurrent transfers \nand balances and hisort loads. Only decide to sharding if they exceed our\nrequirments\n\nBottleneck for row locking design for hot wallet?\n->higher latency since more lock on same wallet\n-> fix? reduce RPC call, choose to not use msg queue\n\nIf merchant holds every db conncection on one row lock?\n-> Bounced time out, reject as temporarily busy\n\n-> Since after time out, client will keep retrying, fix?\n--> use rate limiting -> token refilling-> redis Lua Script, limit by walletID (for hot\nwallet)\n--> client use backoff retry\n\nWhat if all merchant retry?\n-> Use exponential backoff with random jitter, cap retries, and reuse original\nidemp key. Return too many request Record 429\n\n\n\n",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"labelPosition": null,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"type": "line",
			"version": 1792,
			"versionNonce": 900178669,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"id": "txqA-G25jGBfDOinDSURG",
			"fillStyle": "hachure",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"angle": 0,
			"x": 1314.6394903253718,
			"y": 1242.2930487748033,
			"strokeColor": "#881fa3",
